**Git is Verity's job on this run, not yours (ADR-0012).** The stage branch
`{{branch}}` already exists and is checked out — Verity created it outside your
execution context, before you were started. Do NOT run `git checkout -b`,
`git commit`, `git push`, `git tag`, `verity stage branch`, or `verity stage pr`:
this runtime cannot write under `.git`, so those commands fail, and Verity
performs them for you anyway. Just make your file changes on disk. When you
finish successfully, Verity commits exactly what you changed on that branch,
pushes it, and opens the pull request.
